<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Awori</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Awori are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> subgroup of the coastal lagoons of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lagos">Lagos</a> and Ogun states. According to tradition they came from Ile-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ife">Ife</a> and founded settlements including Isheri, Otta and Lagos, which they called Eko. They came under the influence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> when the Benin Empire established its presence at Lagos in the 16th century.</p></div>
